Adaptation: behavior adapted from the description only; no upstream code is
copied, and the DeepSeek Recipe encoder it describes is not in the source tree
(the in-tree eval/run_eval.py:222 encodes the whole prompt text and does not
itself segment). Fak adds a seam-preserving segmented encode to its Go
tokenizer: added and control tokens match only inside trusted template text,
client text between matches stays one BPE chunk across segment seams so benign
prompts keep their ids, and no plain run ever yields an added-token id. The
DeepSeek V4.1 chat renderer marks message content, tool schemas, tool-call
names and arguments, and the response format as client text, and native
prompt encoding uses the segmented path only when
FAK_DEEPSEEK41_SEGMENTED_PROMPT=1 (renderer id suffix +segmented-v1).
Output-side recognition of </think> and DSML by token id is not adapted here.
